    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VWYQfenU8rHfJkKC7ERYoX)_\n\n## What\n\n- `citar-create-note` (so also `citar-embark` opening a `[cite:]` link with no note) now makes the note with `sp-litnotes-meta-create-function`, the same path as the backfill, instead of citar-vulpea.\n  - The note is born compliant: title from `sp-litnotes-meta-new-title`, file named by the key, ID, `:CREATED:`, `litnote` and BibTeX type tags, ROAM_REFS.\n  - It is then filled from BibTeX (when `sp-litnotes-meta-auto`) and visited.\n- The advice is now `:around`. A key that already has a note, has no BibTeX entry, or fails to be made goes to citar as before (with the old fill afterwards).\n- New `sp-litnotes-meta-citar-create` (default t) turns the new route off.\n- `sp-litnotes-meta-new-title` already defaulted to `standard` on main; unchanged.\n- Doc: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org` (bullet list) and tangled `.el`; one ERT test added.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Emacs is not in the container, so neither the new test nor the byte-compile ran. Not tried with real citar/citar-embark.\n- Whether citar-embark's open-notes flow expects `citar-create-note` to return something specific (the new route returns the visiting buffer).\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBbVYKovP8EnbMCTgH)_",
